(Machine Learning Fundamentals) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. What is Machine Learning) Tj
T*
(Machine learning is a branch of artificial intelligence that lets systems) Tj
T*
(learn patterns from data instead of following explicit rules. A machine learning) Tj
T*
(model is a mathematical function trained on examples to make predictions.) Tj
T*
(The quality of the predictions depends on both the algorithm and the data used) Tj
T*
(for training. Machine learning powers applications such as recommendation) Tj
T*
(systems, spam filters, medical diagnosis, and language translation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Types of Machine Learning) Tj
T*
(Supervised learning uses labeled data, where each example has a known answer.) Tj
T*
(Regression predicts a continuous value such as a house price, while) Tj
T*
(classification predicts a category such as spam or not spam. Unsupervised) Tj
T*
(learning finds hidden structure in unlabeled data, for example grouping similar) Tj
T*
(customers using clustering. Reinforcement learning trains an agent to take) Tj
T*
(actions in an environment to maximize a cumulative reward signal.) Tj
T*
(Semi-supervised learning combines a small amount of labeled data with a) Tj
T*
(large amount of unlabeled data to improve accuracy at lower labeling cost.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. The Training Process) Tj
T*
(Training a model means adjusting its parameters so that its predictions) Tj
T*
(match the known answers as closely as possible. The difference between the) Tj
T*
(prediction and the true answer is measured by a loss function. Gradient) Tj
T*
(descent is an optimization algorithm that repeatedly updates the parameters in) Tj
T*
(the direction that reduces the loss. The learning rate controls how large each) Tj
T*
(update step is; a learning rate that is too high causes the loss to diverge,) Tj
T*
(while a learning rate that is too low makes training extremely slow.) Tj
ET
endstream
