(4. Overfitting and Underfitting) Tj
T*
(Overfitting happens when a model memorizes the training data, including its) Tj
T*
(noise, and performs poorly on new unseen data. Underfitting happens when the) Tj
T*
(model is too simple to capture the underlying pattern. The bias-variance) Tj
T*
(tradeoff describes the tension between model simplicity and flexibility.) Tj
T*
(Techniques to reduce overfitting include regularization, dropout, early) Tj
T*
(stopping, and collecting more training data. Cross-validation splits the data) Tj
T*
(into folds to give a more reliable estimate of generalization performance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Evaluating Models) Tj
T*
(Accuracy is the fraction of correct predictions, but it can be misleading on) Tj
T*
(imbalanced datasets. Precision measures how many of the predicted positives) Tj
T*
(are actually correct, while recall measures how many of the real positives the) Tj
T*
(model found. The F1 score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall. For) Tj
T*
(regression tasks, mean squared error penalizes large errors more heavily) Tj
T*
(than mean absolute error does. Confusion matrices summarize true positives,) Tj
T*
(true negatives, false positives, and false negatives for classification models.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Neural Networks) Tj
T*
(A neural network is a model inspired by the structure of the brain. It consists) Tj
T*
(of layers of neurons, where each neuron computes a weighted sum of its inputs) Tj
T*
(and passes the result through an activation function. Hidden layers between the) Tj
T*
(input and output allow the network to learn increasingly abstract features.) Tj
T*
(Backpropagation is the algorithm that computes how much each weight contributed) Tj
T*
(to the loss, so the weights can be updated with gradient descent. Deep learning) Tj
T*
(is the subfield that studies neural networks with many hidden layers.) Tj
T*
(Convolutional neural networks are especially effective for image tasks, while) Tj
T*
(transformer architectures with attention mechanisms dominate modern language) Tj
T*
(models such as large language models.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. Practical Advice for Students) Tj
T*
(Start with a simple baseline model before using complex architectures. Always) Tj
T*
(reserve a held-out test set that the model never sees during training. Log) Tj
T*
(hyperparameters and results so experiments can be compared fairly. Understanding) Tj
T*
(why a model fails is often more valuable than a single high score, because it) Tj
T*
(guides the next improvement.) Tj
ET
